  "id": "COMPOUND:27962 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between n-Octyl sulfate and Raji cells, mediated through the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase enzyme. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, all of which have a final score of 0.5246. These compounds are likely acting as inhibitors of the enzyme, which in turn may influence Raji cell function. The presence of multiple independent pathways pointing to the same target enzyme supports a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a role for n-Octyl sulfate in modulating the activity of this enzyme, potentially affecting Raji cell behavior.",
